"<section id="a-framework-of-principles" class="slide slide-title" data-kind="title" data-line="1">
<h1 class="headline">A framework of principles</h1>
<aside class="notes" data-source="generated">
<p>Perhaps the most important lesson learned through this exercise was that while I do not need to understand the actual code, it is essential to keep testing often and thoroughly. Reflecting on my exploration---and analysing what distinguished successful projects from abandoned ones---led me to five principles that form the basis of a future example document framework:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<strong>Planning:</strong> Thorough planning remains (almost) everything</li>
<li>
<strong>Documenting:</strong> Document from a user perspective, then from a developer perspective</li>
<li>
<strong>Testing:</strong> Use automated and manual testing regularly and consistently</li>
<li>
<strong>Pacing:</strong> If in doubt, slow down to avoid being overwhelmed by complexity</li>
<li>
<strong>Embrace failure:</strong> Vibe coding enables a 'review &amp; resubmit' mentality, use it</li>
</ol>
