exports[`the built deck on every example chapter > examples/talk/01-talk/05-what-i-have-learned.md 1`] = `
"<section id="what-i-have-learned" class="slide slide-divider divider" data-kind="divider" data-line="1">
<h1 class="headline">What I have learned ...</h1>
<aside class="notes" data-source="authored">
<p>While I do not need to understand the actual code, it is essential to keep testing often and thoroughly. The speed-quality trade-off paradox: vibe coders experience rapid "instant success and flow," yet most perceive the resulting code as fast but flawed.</p>
</aside>
</section>
<section id="slide" class="slide slide-continuation" data-kind="continuation" data-line="9">
<div class="face">
<figure class="full-bleed">
<img src="assets/lineage-timeline.svg" />
</figure>
</div>
<aside class="notes" data-source="authored">
<p>Total Lines Modified</p>
<p>Cumulative LOC growth over time by lineage. Triangle markers indicate first commits; circles indicate releases; bubble size reflects feature count. Grey lines show other lineages for context.</p>
<p>For ragged:</p>
<ul>
<li>Final codebase size: 134,090 LOC (actual lines in repo)</li>
<li>Cumulative LOC changed: 569,890 LOC (sum of all additions + deletions over time)</li>
</ul>
<p>Why It Inflates</p>
<ol>
<li>Deletions count as changes - Removing 10K lines adds 10K to the cumulative total</li>
<li>Refactoring double-counts - Moving code = deletion + addition = 2× the lines</li>
<li>Rewrites accumulate - Each iteration adds to the total, even if replacing existing code</li>
</ol>
</aside>
</section>
<section id="slide-2" class="slide slide-image" data-kind="image" data-line="30">
<div class="face">
<figure class="full-bleed">
<img src="assets/codebase-overview.svg" />
</figure>
</div>
<aside class="notes" data-source="authored">
<p>Codebase size (LOC) and feature counts by repository. Colour indicates lineage. Note correlation between codebase size and documented features in production projects.</p>
</aside>
</section>
<section id="slide-3" class="slide slide-image" data-kind="image" data-line="36">
<div class="face">
<figure class="full-bleed">
<img src="assets/feature-density.svg" />
</figure>
</div>
<aside class="notes" data-source="authored">
<p>Feature documentation density normalised to maximum. Shows features per 1000 LOC. Foundation projects show "No feature docs"; production projects demonstrate consistent documentation practices regardless of codebase size.</p>
</aside>
</section>
<section id="slide-4" class="slide slide-image" data-kind="image" data-line="42">
<div class="face">
<figure class="full-bleed">
<img src="assets/file-composition.svg" />
</figure>
</div>
<aside class="notes" data-source="authored">
<p>Pie charts showing Source/Test/Docs breakdown for each repository. Percentages and file counts displayed. Illustrates varying emphasis on documentation across project maturity levels.</p>
</aside>
</section>
<section id="slide-5" class="slide slide-image" data-kind="image" data-line="48">
<div class="face">
<figure class="full-bleed">
<img src="assets/knowledge-inheritance.svg" />
</figure>
</div>
<aside class="notes" data-source="authored">
<p>Knowledge transfer between project iterations. Shows what percentage of Code, Architecture, Testing, and Documentation was kept, modified, or dropped. Demonstrates learning progression within each lineage.</p>
</aside>
</section>"
`;

